{"id": "255e3a8d-d2ef-435d-8d5a-ba7ae2a31045", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll pull cost data from Cost Explorer comparing August and September, broken down by service and by linked account, to find what's driving the 18% increase.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_vExMJZ9NjkexiZkKyQwUcS", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Explain what drove an ~18% increase in total AWS bill from August to September. Break down the increase by AWS service and by linked account.",
  "context": "User sees total AWS spend was about 18% higher in September vs August and wants to know which services and which accounts are responsible for the increase. They have Cost Explorer and CUR enabled, so use Cost Explorer's GetCostAndUsage API (grouped by SERVICE and by LINKED_ACCOUNT) for August (2026-08-01 to 2026-09-01) and September (2026-09-01 to 2026-10-01), using UnblendedCost. Compute month-over-month dollar and percent change per service and per account, and surface the top contributors to the overall increase (e.g. top 5-8 services and top accounts by absolute dollar delta). Call out any new services/accounts that appeared in September that weren't in August, and any one-time anomalies if visible (e.g. a spike concentrated in a few days within September, checked via daily granularity if helpful).",
  "resources": ["Cost Explorer GetCostAndUsage API", "all linked accounts in the organization/agent space"],
  "timeframe": "2026-08-01T00:00:00Z/2026-10-01T00:00:00Z",
  "criteria": "Identify top services and accounts by absolute dollar increase and percent increase from August to September. Total monthly cost for August and September. Confirm the overall percent increase matches roughly 18%. Flag any single service/account that accounts for a disproportionate share of the increase."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Query Cost Explorer for August vs September cost breakdown by service and account."}], "created_at": null}
